# Ghost Data Still Exists: a deletion-audit agent

For every deletion request the agent decides whether the person really asked for deletion, then reconstructs what actually exists at the case's `audit_at` time from the evidence files (SQL snapshots and replicas, JSON exports, six log formats, PDFs, screenshots) and reports `COMPLETE`, `INCOMPLETE` or `NOT_APPLICABLE`.
For an incomplete deletion it lists the remaining records and recreation risks, an ordered remediation plan and the checks that must pass afterwards, all cited to evidence captured at or before `audit_at`.
A deterministic engine does the matching, state reconstruction, policy and planning; language models are used only for three narrow jobs (intake, screenshot transcription, and resolving ambiguous record links) and every model answer goes through code that can reject it.

