## Quickstart

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate            # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r code/requirements.txt   # same list as ./requirements.txt; ships in code.zip
# put the challenge's dataset/ folder at the repository root (next to code/), then:
python code/main.py run --split full   # writes output.csv at the repository root
```

This works with **no API keys and no network**: the default mode replays the committed case-agent decisions and every other model answer (intake labels, screenshot transcriptions) from `code/cache/`, so this exact command reproduces the submitted `output.csv` byte for byte (sha256 `{{final.output_short}}…`, checked in a clean room, see [SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md](code/docs/SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md)). `--mode agent` allows live model calls for routed cases without a stored answer (keys required); `--mode deterministic` runs without the case agent.

Optional live model access (copy `.env.example` to `.env`; never commit `.env`):

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `GROQ_API_KEY` | Groq key for the case agent |
| `GROQ_MODEL`, `GROQ_FALLBACK_MODEL` | primary and fallback Groq models (`openai/gpt-oss-120b`, `openai/gpt-oss-20b`) |
| `GROQ_EXTRA_MODELS` | optional comma-separated extra Groq models tried after the fallback (read by `llm.agent_chain`) |
| `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_MODEL` | Gemini key and model (vision, intake, last-resort agent model) |

Other commands: `python code/main.py run --split sample`, `python code/main.py tools` (tool registry), `python code/main.py explain case_11` (why a case came out as it did). A Makefile wraps the common ones (`make help`).

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  subgraph GLOBAL[Global phase, then the run context is frozen]
    EV[EvidenceAgent: parsers + cached Gemini vision] --> IN[IntakeAgent: rules + LLM labels]
    IN --> GA[InvestigatorAgent.global_assign: learned worker windows, tie groups]
  end
  GA --> ID
  subgraph CASE[Per case: isolated, one retry]
    ID[IdentityAgent: current + historical identity] --> LK[InvestigatorAgent.link: key, catalog, worker window, propagation, stale filter]
    LK --> AS[AssessorAgent: treatment + state at audit_at]
    AS --> PL[PlannerAgent: deterministic plan = default and fallback]
    PL --> VF[VerifierAgent: output contract]
    VF --> RT[RouterAgent: open linking decisions?]
  end
  RT -->|none: fast path| W
  RT -->|tie_break / tie_lost / skip_multi / identity_conflict| CI[CaseInvestigatorAgent: LLM tool loop, max 8 calls]
  CI --> GATE[Deterministic gate: propose_plan = planner + validator]
  GATE --> GC[Global consistency check]
  GC --> VF2[VerifierAgent on changed rows]
  VF2 --> W[Writer: validated output.csv, run_summary.json, traces]
```

The planner runs for every case before the router decides, because the deterministic plan is both the default (every ambiguity keeps its default) and the fallback when the agent fails, runs out of budget or is rejected. `propose_plan` calls that same planner, so the agent can only choose between link sets; it never writes steps. Details: [ARCHITECTURE.md](code/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), tool table: [TOOLS.md](code/docs/TOOLS.md).

One routed case:

```mermaid
