## Limitations and next steps

- **Ties are undecidable without more evidence.** When several cases fit a worker event equally, `SKIP_MULTI` leaves the resource unassigned ({{linker.skip_multi_groups}} such groups on the full split); on the sample this leaves {{sample.taxonomy.ties}} gold steps missing, and the {{sample.taxonomy.tie_guesses}} wrong steps are tie-break guesses ({{tiebreak.rows.SKIP_MULTI.ties_sample_correct}} of {{tiebreak.rows.SKIP_MULTI.ties_sample}} sample tie-breaks were right).
- **Audit records absent from every input** cannot be recovered (the sample has {{sample.taxonomy.unrecoverable}} such steps).
- **Assumed-compliant records.** {{linker.blind.assumed_compliant}} of {{linker.linked_resources}} linked full-split resources ({{linker.blind.share}}) have no capture at or before `audit_at`; {{linker.blind.only_after_audit}} are seen only afterwards, and {{linker.blind.later_violation}} of those are shown in violation by a later file but cannot be used to decide state.
- **Free-tier budget.** The LLM agent covers only as many routed cases as the free quotas allow in the time box; the rest use the deterministic default. See [usage_report.md](code/evaluation/usage_report.md).

## How this was built

Built with Claude Code under the `AGENTS.md` protocol: every session turn is logged in `log.txt` (the chat transcript submitted with this repository). The design decisions were made by the author and are recorded with their evidence in [DECISIONS.md](code/docs/DECISIONS.md); the AI wrote most of the code under those specifications and under test-first constraints (every module has tests built from real dataset rows, behavior-preserving refactors are guarded by the golden lock, and logic changes are measured with the evaluation harness).
